what_this_closes:
T0182 landed the mechanism with the OLD pull_request triggers still in place, because workflow_dispatch only fires for a workflow already on the DEFAULT BRANCH -- the delivery that adds the mechanism cannot be validated by it. That constraint is discharged the moment T0182 merges, and this delivery removes the daytime cycle:

  * no gate runs on pull_request;
  * phase4 and phase5 no longer run a full gate on every push to phase/**;
  * push remains only for master.

The register declares NIGHTLY_AUTHORITATIVE_VALIDATION, and the transitional NIGHTLY_MODEL_LANDING value is DELETED from the validator's accepted set rather than left available: a transition value that outlives its transition is just a way to switch the checks off. Proven -- setting the register back to the landing value now fails with 'the only accepted value is NIGHTLY_AUTHORITATIVE_VALIDATION'.
